Sval: the RFP window-rounding tests read the content area as it settles

Backport of Mozilla's Bug 2054792 (mozilla-central a2152ea74bfb, Firefox
155), tests only, unchanged. It includes the change Bug 1710902
(mozilla-central 524bf09b055a, Firefox 154) made to the same two files,
which replaces BrowserTestUtils.waitForCondition with
TestUtils.waitForCondition and which Bug 2054792's hunks build on. ESR 153
carries neither.
browser_dynamical_window_rounding.js compared the content read after a
resize with a rounding of the browser container's size read once before it,
and on Linux resized again until the container matched the requested outer
width, which it never does when the chrome beside the page takes part of the
window's width, as Sval's workspace panel does. The test re-reads the
container in its wait and waits for the rounding to settle, on every
platform. browser_roundedWindow_newWindow.js asserts that RFP's spoofed
screen, available screen and inner sizes are one positive size, where it
re-derived a pixel size that holds only for small chrome.
Drop this patch when the upstream pin reaches Firefox 155.

